# DWT folder structure

The layout, new version steps and naming conventions are in `general/file-structure-and-versioning.mdc`. That file describes this repo — follow it. This file adds project-specific points only.

- Structure is by **version** (`v1`–`v4`), then by **section** (`regulators/`, `software-providers/`). There are no phase or feature hubs, and no `designs.html` pages.
- `app/views/index.html` is the only hub. Every new version needs a card there and a `versions/vN.html` page — don't leave new work unlinked.
- Shared partials are allowed but are per version, with a leading underscore (e.g. `v4/software-providers/_email-addresses.html`, included with `{% include version + "/software-providers/_email-addresses.html" %}`). Copy them into the new version rather than pointing at an older one.
- Versions intentionally duplicate near-identical pages (`v3/` and `v4/` are copies). Follow the pattern rather than unifying them, unless asked.
- `v1` and `v2` are the research versions — treat as frozen.
- Links to something not built point to the `placeholder.html` page in that version's folder (only `v1` and `v2` have one, rendered by the "dead links" route in `routes.js`). Copy it into a new version if you need it. Don't use `#` or a dead link.
- `app/views/versions/vN.html` and `app/views/index.html` extend `layouts/prototype-hub.html`, not the in-service layout.

## Creating new work

- New version → follow "Starting a new version" in the general file.
- New page in an existing version → `.html` in the relevant section folder, extending that version's layout, with `version`, `pageName` and `activeSection` set. Add its routes inside that version's `registerVNRoutes()`.
- New section → new folder inside the version, plus a navigation item in `layouts/vN.html`.
- No design yet → use the placeholder pattern above.
